module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FinitePresentation
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.BaseChangeConventions

/-!
# Pointwise descent of local finite presentation along a field extension

Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tag 0C4Y, and the affine-local definition of local
finite presentation (blueprint: lem-sc-lfp-field-extension-pointwise-descent).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Local finite presentation near a point descends along a field extension.
Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tag 0C4Y, combined with the affine-local definition;
there is no single Stacks tag for this pointwise formulation
(blueprint: lem-sc-lfp-field-extension-pointwise-descent).

Proof:
1. Choose affine charts Spec B around x and Spec A around f(x). Choose a principal
open D(v) around xK inside the given neighbourhood. The algebra (B tensor K)_v is
finitely presented over A tensor K by lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation.
2. Descend surjectivity of a C-module map from D(v) in Spec(C tensor K) to D(c)
around its image: the projection is open by lem-sc-scheme-over-field-universally-open.
At each prime in that image, its local ring map is flat and local by
lem-weil-pbc-field-extension-base-change-faithfully-flat and Tag 0C4Y. Reflect
surjectivity using lem-pc-local-flat-faithful-flat-reflects-surjective, then use
surjectivity at all primes to obtain surjectivity on D(c).
3. Generate an A-subalgebra B' by the finitely many coefficients occurring in v
and in generators of (B tensor K)_v. Flatness embeds B' tensor K in B tensor K.
Apply step 2 to B' into B to obtain a finitely generated algebra B_c near x.
4. Present this algebra as a quotient of A[t_1,...,t_n] by I. After scalar extension
and localization, adjoining an inverse to a lift of v gives a finitely presented
algebra. Its kernel is finitely generated by
lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-surjection-kernel-fg. Choose finitely many elements
of I whose scalar extensions generate the localized kernel, giving an ideal J.
Apply step 2 to J into I to get J localized equal to I localized near x.
The resulting B_s is finitely presented over A.
5. D(s) is an open neighbourhood of x on which f is locally of finite presentation
by def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation. -/
theorem locallyOfFinitePresentation_near_of_fieldExtension
    (k K : Type u) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (X Y : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))) (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : X.left) :
    let i := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K))
    ∀ (xK : ↥(pullback X.hom i)), pullback.fst X.hom i xK = x →
      (∃ W : (pullback X.hom i).Opens, xK ∈ W ∧
        LocallyOfFinitePresentation (W.ι ≫ ((Over.pullback i).map f).left)) →
      ∃ U : X.left.Opens, x ∈ U ∧ LocallyOfFinitePresentation (U.ι ≫ f.left) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
